    {
      "id": "f8853e10-6662-4ec1-93f6-c2afa92f0d57",
      "name": "Sticky Note a5b05501",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Automation 04: Lead Capture and Routing\n\n### Introduction\nLogs each new enquiry, assigns one rep by country and postal code, and replies to the prospect within seconds. No AI is used.\n\n### What to key in\nThe prospect fills in **Lead Form**: name, email, phone, company, country, postal code, budget, enquiry and PDPA consent.\nStaff keep reps in the **Territories** tab: country, postal_prefix (blank means the whole country), rep details and active (yes or no).\nAfter contact, the rep sets status to Contacted in the **Leads** tab.\n\n### What happens next\n1. Spam is logged and stopped. The form has basic filters only, with no CAPTCHA.\n2. A repeat email within 90 days goes to the existing rep, not a second one.\n3. A new lead goes to the matching rep, sharing evenly if several match.\n4. No match goes to the fallback rep in **Config**.\n5. The rep gets the lead details, and the prospect gets the rep contact card.\n6. Each weekday at 9am, reps are reminded about leads not contacted within 24 hours.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect your Gmail account in all four Gmail nodes.\n2. In **Config**, enter company_name and the fallback rep.\n3. Test with test_mode on in **Config** and **Reminder Config**, which sends every email to test_email.\n4. For live use, set test_mode to false in both, then publish.\n5. Share the Production URL from **Lead Form**.",
        "color": 4,
        "width": 680,
        "height": 800
      }
    }
